# Clover's XNU patch series (format 2).
#
# What this board's kernel is built from is the whole set the format-1 tree accumulated: every
# base patch plus the two XnuPrelink patches, in the alphabetical order the format-1 build applied
# them. That is not an accident of history worth trimming here. The format-1 build's LATE_PATCH
# loop (scripts/build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh) tries to reverse the newest clover diagnostics before
# each build, but its first entry is the r331 patch, and round335 rewrote that patch after it had
# been applied -- so the reverse check fails on the first entry, every later reverse is skipped
# for want of that context, and the loop is a no-op. The shipped r344 kernel still prints the
# r308/r309/r327/r328/r331 rows (boot 124's card), so those kernel patches are inside the image,
# not reverted. Listing them here says what the build actually does instead of relying on a loop
# that silently does nothing.
#
# Replaying exactly these 140 patches on a pristine d8b80295 checkout reproduces the r344 XNU work
# tree with zero differing files (the only extra files are the public headers
# scripts/prepare-xnu-source.py adds).
#
# Do not swap this for the arch profile series plus the device patches: the arch series is a
# 56-entry subset that misses native-smp-secondary (8 CPUs) and sheng-platform-power, and it also
# carries three newer patches (native-4k-signature-hash-cache, offline-owner-root-binding-audit,
# offline-owner-systemos-mount) whose hunks collide with the clover diagnostics, so that
# combination stops applying at r226. This file is self-contained for the same reason.
#
# Paths: `arch:` is the arch profile root (<repo>/profiles/arch/arm64); three levels up is the
# repository root, so `arch:../../../patches/xnu/NAME` is <repo>/patches/xnu/NAME. The two
# kit patches come from the XnuPrelink component. boot-progress stays even though this board
# builds XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS=n: the r344 tree had it applied and its hooks compile away when the
# flag is off.

